course: dictionary
lesson: 11961
title: Words for groups and classes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a group that people or animals belong to. «Caste» is one of these words. It names a group that someone is born into, so you do not choose it.
explain: «In the old caste system, a child's job was decided by the group they were born into.» The clue is "born into": a caste is where you are placed at birth. Here it describes people in history and religion.
explain: «The worker caste in an ant colony digs tunnels and carries food.» Now caste means a group of insects that each do one kind of job. Check it: "a group of workers who dig and carry" fits the sentence, so caste means a group with a job.
fact: A caste is a group someone is born into, which in the past decided their work and who they could marry.
fact: The caste system is best known from the traditional system in India and Nepal, and it is linked to Hindu society in South Asia.
fact: Caste discrimination is against the law in India, though it still affects many lives.
fact: In an insect colony, a caste is a group that does one kind of job, such as workers, soldiers or the queen.
fact: Useful phrases: «caste system», «lower caste», «worker caste».
exercise: «In the old caste system, a child's job was decided by the group they were born into.» What does caste mean here? | *A group someone is born into, which decided their work | A type of hat worn in the past | A fast way to travel | A kind of school test
exercise: «The worker caste in an ant colony digs tunnels and carries food.» What kind of group is a caste here? | *A group of insects that each do one kind of job | A type of food ants like | A group of ants who all sleep in one place | A king who rules the colony
exercise: Ravi says a caste is a fixed social class that is hard to move out of. Is he right? | *Yes, that is one meaning of caste | No, caste only means a type of ant | No, caste means a race of horses | No, a caste is always a sweet
test: What does the phrase «caste system» refer to? | A game played with cards | A school timetable | A way of counting money | *A traditional system of social groups people are born into, best known from India and Nepal
test: «In a bee colony, the queen belongs to a caste with one special job.» In this sentence, caste means? | A bee's wings | *A group of insects in a colony that do one kind of job | A type of honey | A sweet smell
exam: Which sentence uses caste correctly? | The soup was a caste of carrots and peas | The caste ran fast around the track | We put the caste on the shelf after lunch | *Because of the family she was born into, Mia was held back, as if she were stuck in her caste
